SUMMARY:The Toronto-London Philosophy of Perception Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Speakers\nJames Stazicker (Kings College London) \nFrances Egan (Rutgers – New Brunswick) \nPeter Epstein (Brandeis University) \nGabriel Greenberg (University of California\, Los Angeles) \nAndrew Y. Lee (University of Toronto) \nAdrienne Prettyman (Bryn Mawr College) \nFriday\, November 13\n\n\n\n9:30 am – 10:00 am\nWelcome\n\n\n10:00 am – 12:00 pm\nPeter Epstein (Brandeis University) \n“Qualia and Ganzfeld Experience”\n\n\n12:00 pm – 1:30 pm\nLunch\n\n\n1:30 pm – 3:30 pm\nJames Stazicker (Kings College London) \n“The Autonomy of Subjective Representation”\n\n\n4:00 pm – 6:00 pm\nAndrew Lee (University of Toronto) \n“The Structure of Iconic Representation”\n\n\n\nSaturday\, November 14\n  \n\n\n\n9:30 am – 10:00 am\nCoffee\n\n\n10:00 am – 12:00 pm\nFrances Egan (Rutgers University) \n“Defending Sortal Adverbialism”\n\n\n12:00 pm – 1:30 pm\nLunch\n\n\n1:30 pm – 3:30 pm\nGabe Greenberg (University of California\, Los Angeles) \n“Neural Images: On Retinotopy and Representation”\n\n\n4:00 pm – 6:00 pm\nAdrienne Prettyman (Bryn Mawr College) \n“Success without Accuracy”\n\n\n\nOrganizers\nSonia Sedivy (University of Toronto)\, Jacob Beck (York University)\, Bill Brewer (King’s College London)\, Kevin J. Lande (York University)\, Matthew Soteriou (University of Pittsburgh)\, and James Stazicker (King’s College London).
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/the-toronto-london-philosophy-of-perception-workshop/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building 100
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/Toronto-London-Workshop-Poster92-300-h.png
END:VEVENT
