UID:35592-1796310000-1796317200@philosophy.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Colloquium (Olivia Bailey\, UC Berkeley)
DESCRIPTION:The Department is pleased to welcome Olivia Bailey\, an assistant professor in the Department of Philosophy\, at UC Berkeley for a colloquium on December 3\, 2026. She works on questions in moral psychology and the history of moral philosophy (particularly the British moralists). Her current research is concerned with the ethical and epistemic significance of empathy. \nTitle\nThe See-Through Heart: Transparency\, Rationality\, and Emotional Self-Knowledge \nAbstract\nHow can I arrive at an answer to the question of how I feel? I could study my behavior\, or defer to my psychoanalyst. But it is hard to resist the idea that there is another way that I—and I alone—can speak to the question of what I feel\, one that does not rely on such indirect observational routes. One potentially powerful lead\, here\, is the fact that I can ordinarily expect my thinking about my feelings to make a difference to what I feel. Perhaps it is no coincidence that I have both a special way to answer the question of how I feel and a special power to shape my feelings through thought. \nI consider two established ways of developing this lead\, an interpretationist view and a transparency view\, and draw out problems for both I then look to the phenomenology of emotional experience for help developing a hybrid of the two that avoids both sets of problems. On this account\, my (and yet special) ordinary authority to say what my emotion is hinges on my power to ‘make up my heart’ by settling a question about the relationship between my inner state and the world.
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/colloquium-olivia-bailey-uc-berkeley/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building 100
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/Olivia-Bailey-325-x-225.png
END:VEVENT
