UID:36326-1796396400-1796403600@philosophy.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Kant & Post-Kantian German Philosophy Group Talk (Giuliano Infantino)
DESCRIPTION:The Kant & Post-Kantian German Philosophy Research Interest Group is pleased to welcome as a speaker\, Giuliano Infantino\, a Feodor Lynen Research Fellow (Alexander von Humboldt Foundation) at the University of Toronto. He completed his PhD at the University of Stuttgart in 2026 and works on German Idealism\, modal metaphysics\, and philosophy of nature. \nTalk Title\nHegel’s Proof of the Necessary Existence of Nature \nTalk Abstract\nThe transition from pure thought to nature is widely regarded as one of the most obscure points of Hegel’s mature system. Hegel claims that philosophy has to prove that there is nature\, and yet he denies that anything becomes of the logical Idea at the end of the Logic. Readers have therefore taken the transition either as an account of how thought produces nature or as a mere change of philosophical discipline. I argue that it is best understood as a modal-metaphysical proof of existence: thought exists necessarily\, and thought could not exist unless there were nature. The crucial premise rests on the self-consciousness of thought. Since the being of thought’s determinations consists in their being known\, and thought cannot know itself as an internally differentiated whole\, its complete self-transparency at the end of the Logic threatens its own existence. I show that the existence of thought therefore depends on a realm which is not logical\, its determinate opposite: nature. I conclude that nature exists necessarily\, although no particular thing in nature does.
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/kant-post-kantian-german-philosophy-group-talk-giuliano-infantino/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building\, Room 418\, 170 St. George Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 2M8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/Giuliano-Infantino-post-doc-cropped-3.png
END:VEVENT
