SUMMARY:Global Philosophy Research Interest Group Talk (Jeannie Miller\, University of Toronto)
DESCRIPTION:The Global Philosophy Research Interest Group is delighted to welcome as guest speaker Jeannie Miller\, an associate professor in the Department of Near and Middle Eastern Studies at the University of Toronto. Her book\, The Quibbler: Al-Jahiz’s Equivocations in Kitab al-Hayawan and Beyond is a study of the Arabic writings of al-Jahiz\, a foundational 9th-century author and analyzes al-Jahiz’s literary style and unique voice as a performative demonstration of good thinking\, according to his definition. She is currently working on several interconnected studies of the reception and afterlife of Abbasid texts in premodern Islamicate contexts\, using manuscripts as evidence. How were these texts read before the modernizing movements of the 19th and 20th centuries and the advent of a modern notion of “literature”? \nTitle\nTBA \nAbstract\nTBA
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/global-philosophy-research-interest-group-talk-jeannie-miller-university-of-toronto/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building\, Room 418\, 170 St. George Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 2M8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/Jeannie-Miller-cropped.png
END:VEVENT
