SUMMARY:Language\, Epistemology\, Metaphysics\, and Mind Research Interest Group (David Bulles\, Princeton)
DESCRIPTION:The Language\, Epistemology\, Metaphysics\, and Mind Research Interest Group is delighted to welcome as guest speaker David Bulles\, an associated professor in the Department of Philosophy at Princeton. He has broad research interests in metaphysics and epistemology. In metaphysics\, he is interested in questions about time\, consciousness\, the self\, laws of nature\, ontology\, infinity\, modality\, explanation\, and fundamentality. In epistemology\, he is interested in the problem of induction\, principles of indifference\, objective chance\, and self-locating belief. \nTalk Title\nTBD \nTalk Abstract\nTBD
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/language-epistemology-metaphysics-and-mind-research-interest-group-david-bulles-princeton/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building\, Room 418\, 170 St. George Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 2M8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/d._builes_hs_2026_-too-high-crop.png
